sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 10-chat-request-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle From the client's HTTPS call to the response, through edge limits, authentication, policy, PII masking, routing, and telemetry
  %% @type cloud: TR
  %% @type security: PR
  %% @type external: D3 OAI
  %% @type database: OBS
  actor C as Client
  participant TR as Traefik<br/>TLS + edge limits
  participant LL as LiteLLM proxy<br/>auth · policy · routing
  participant PR as Presidio<br/>PII masking
  participant D3 as D3-mini<br/>remote GPU host
  participant OAI as OpenAI<br/>provider model
  participant OBS as Telemetry<br/>spend · metrics · spans

  C->>TR: POST /v1/chat/completions over HTTPS
  alt over the runaway-client limits
    TR--xC: 429 Too Many Requests
  else within limits
    TR->>LL: route by host
    alt key invalid or model not allowed
      LL--xC: 401 / 403 through Traefik
    else authorized
      Note over LL: resolve the eu-data-protection policy
      LL->>PR: pre_call: mask PII in the input
      PR-->>LL: masked input
      opt model is coding-router
        LL->>D3: classify the request (routing sequence)
        D3-->>LL: tier
      end
      LL->>OAI: call the provider model
      OAI-->>LL: completion
      LL->>PR: post_call: mask PII in the output
      PR-->>LL: masked output
      LL-)OBS: spend log, metrics, content-free span
      LL-->>TR: response
      TR-->>C: response
    end
  end
